    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute goes to a human reviewer. No money is collected or refunded now; the 4.20 SGD the rider contests is held.\n\nThe established facts. The trip record (EV-TRIP-05014, weight 1.0) records 10.9 km against a recommended 9.6 km — a deviation of 1.30 km, over the 1.0 km tolerance (POL-RD-22, POL-RD-24). The LTA advisory (EV-ADVIS-05014-01) reports an ACCIDENT on the KPE towards TPE after the MacPherson Road exit, inside the trip window; the recommended route runs on the KPE in that direction, so the advisory intersects the route and the reroute was traffic-justified (POL-RD-23). The driver's in-app message at 21:19:56 named both the reason and the reroute, before the deviation detected at 21:22:26, so the rider was informed (POL-RD-21).\n\nThe open question. POL-RD-24 row (a) needs the rider to have agreed; row (b) needs her not informed; and the clause sends a case that fits no row to escalation. The rider's only reply, MSG-05014-004 — 'aiyo can meh... ok lor whatever u say but dun charge me more ah' — mixes assent with a condition on the fare. The chat log (EV-CHAT-05014) is impaired at weight 0.85 with issue code LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY, and the pre-pass records the reply as ambiguous between acknowledgment and objection, so agreement is not established (POL-GEN-26).\n\nThe confidence bar. The rider's profile carries a fraud flag (EV-RPROF-05014), which fixes the confidence an AI ruling needs at 0.95 (POL-GEN-22). The fact that would decide row (a) — the rider's acknowledgment — is carried only by the impaired chat at 0.85, so confidence cannot reach 0.95 and POL-RD-25 requires escalation.\n\nOn the arguments. The driver's points that the reroute was traffic-justified, that the rider was informed before the deviation, and that the deviation was 1.30 km are accepted, as is his point that no ruling can reach 0.95 on an 0.85 artifact; his claim that the trip record independently carries the notice is rejected, because that block derives from the same messages and carries no content, and his row (a) no-refund case is rejected because agreement is not established. The rider's points that the deviation is 1.30 km and that her reply is conditional rather than an acknowledgment are accepted; her claim that the traffic justification fails and row (d) applies is rejected, because the advisory's blank intersection field is left for me to decide, and on its road (KPE), direction (towards TPE) and location (after the MacPherson Road exit) it lies on the recommended route. The most a route-deviation refund could reach is the excess distance fare, 1.30 km x 0.72 SGD/km = 0.94 SGD (EV-FARE-05014), well below the 4.20 SGD she asked, but no refund row fits on this record so that sum is not ordered. The rider is not simply left carrying the charge either: NO_ACTION is not the outcome, because the case escalates and the amount is held pending human review."
