    "explanation": "The route deviation itself is established. The trip record's recorded distances are 10.9 km actual against 9.6 km recommended, a deviation of 1.30 km, over the 1.0 km tolerance (POL-RD-22); the trace is not used to re-measure distance, and the 30-second GPS trace confirms the vehicle left the KPE at the MacPherson Road exit at 21:22:26 and rejoined at Hougang Avenue 3 at 21:34:06. The reroute is traffic-justified (POL-RD-23): the LTA ACCIDENT advisory on the Kallang-Paya Lebar Expressway towards TPE after the MacPherson Road exit is valid 21:06-22:16, covering the trip window 21:16-21:38, and lies on the KPE stretch the recommended route traverses, so I decide its undetermined intersects_route limb in the driver's favour. The driver did inform the rider before deviating: his in-app message MSG-05014-003 at 21:19:56 gave the reason and the intended reroute, two and a half minutes before the 21:22:26 deviation (POL-RD-21). The driver's counterparty statement, 'I asked the passenger and she said ok', is self-serving and is not one of the routes of notice POL-RD-21 names, so it establishes nothing on its own.\n\nWhat cannot be settled is whether the rider agreed. That turns on her reply MSG-05014-004 at 21:20:41, 'aiyo can meh... ok lor whatever u say but dun charge me more ah', which the pre-pass reads as mixing assent with a condition on the fare. Only the chat log carries the reply's content, and it is impaired: EV-CHAT-05014, weight 0.85, issue code LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY (POL-GEN-02(3)). The trip record's messages_during_trip block carries that messages occurred at those times, but not their words, so the acknowledgment still rests on the impaired chat log alone. Row (a) of POL-RD-24 needs the rider informed and agreed; row (b) needs her not informed, and she plainly was informed. Whether she agreed is undecided, and POL-RD-24 names exactly this middle case - 'informed but the rider objected' - as one that fits no row and escalates under POL-GEN-26.\n\nThe confidence rule compels the same end. The acknowledgment is carried solely by the impaired chat log, so the cap under POL-GEN-02(2) is 0.85. Because the rider's profile carries fraud_flags = 1, POL-GEN-22 requires a confidence of 0.95 whatever the amount, and POL-RD-25 gives an AI ruling no standing below its bar. 0.85 cannot reach 0.95, so no monetary decision issues.\n\nOn the parties' submissions. Rider: the 1.30 km deviation and the 0.94 SGD excess-distance fare (1.30 x 0.72 per km, no surge, POL-RD-24) are the correct figures, but the remedy is not ripe; her submission that the reroute is not traffic-justified is rejected for the reason given above; her point that NO_ACTION is party-relative and would leave her carrying the charge is well taken, but no refund can be ordered either. Driver: traffic justification and timely notice are accepted; his reading of the reply as an acknowledgment is not established at the required standard; his submission that a refund order cannot stand at 0.95 confidence is well taken and is the basis of this ruling; and his ceiling of 0.94 SGD is the most any row could return, far short of the 4.20 SGD contested.\n\nThe 4.20 SGD contested is therefore held, not collected and not refunded. The human reviewer should decide whether 'ok lor whatever u say but dun charge me more ah' amounts to the rider's acknowledgment of the reroute under POL-RD-21: if it does, row (a) applies and nothing is refunded; if it does not, the case remains one that fits no row."
