    "explanation": "To both parties. This dispute cannot be decided by the AI and goes to a human reviewer. The 4.20 SGD the rider contests (POL-GEN-22 value; POL-GEN-03) is held rather than collected or refunded.\n\nWhat the record establishes. The deviation is 1.30 km: the platform trip record gives actual 10.9 km against recommended 9.6 km (EV-TRIP-05014), and POL-RD-22 fixes that as the recorded distances and forbids re-measuring from the sparse trace (EV-GPS-05014's 9.226 km understates the route). That is over the 1.0 km tolerance.\n\nThe reroute was traffic-justified (POL-RD-23). EV-ADVIS-05014-01 is an LTA ACCIDENT advisory — an 'incident' type in the admissible list — on the KPE towards TPE after the MacPherson Road exit, valid 21:06:05 to 22:16:05, covering the 21:16:05–21:38:05 trip window. The recommended route runs on the KPE (EV-TRIP-05014 optimal_route_via) and the vehicle left it at the MacPherson Road exit at 21:22:26, so the advisory sits on the stretch of KPE the recommended route would have used; the driver's own message reports the accident 'on KPE ahead'. The rider's argument that the advisory's blank intersects_route field defeats justification is not accepted: that field was expressly left to the judge, and the road, direction and location resolve it for the driver.\n\nThe driver informed the rider (POL-RD-21). MSG-05014-003 at 21:19:56 gave a brief reason and named the reroute, 2 min 30 s before the deviation at 21:22:26, and the timing is also in the trip record's messages_during_trip block.\n\nThe open question, and why the AI cannot rule. The only rider reply, MSG-05014-004 at 21:20:41 — 'aiyo can meh... ok lor whatever u say but dun charge me more ah' — mixes assent with a condition on the fare. The pre-pass graded it IMPAIRED at weight 0.85 with issue LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY (POL-GEN-02(3)), and I read it the same way: it does not clearly confirm the rider's acknowledgment, so POL-RD-21 does not make the deviation 'agreed', but neither is it